@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@
 Blessed be ye *poor*: for yours is the *kingdom of God*.
 ____
 
-Why should an empty wallet inherit a kingdom?
+Why should the poor inherit a kingdom?
 It should not, and it does not — because the wallet was never the measure.
 Among the Hebrew words rendered __“poor”__ in these promises is a close family also rendered __“meek”__ and __“humble”__ — Strong’s calls its two chief members __“practically the same”__ — and the family grows from a root that means _bowed down_.
 The poor of the promises are the bowed.
